cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these fixtures, cite LBFGSpp, Eigen and the biharmonic coordinates, which produce them.
title: Cage-fit oracle generator (host-native test, not vendored)
abstract: >-
  gen.cpp is written here; nothing is vendored. build.sh clones
  V-Sekai-fire/interactor-aria-lbfgspp at the pinned commit (LBFGSpp 0.3.0, MIT;
  Eigen 3.4.90, MPL-2.0) and V-Sekai-fire/interactor-tool-godot-cage-deformer at
  the pinned commit (src/BHC.h and src/point3.h, MIT) into .deps/ (gitignored),
  and compiles gen.cpp against them unmodified. The only local adaptation is
  wrapping the LBFGSB.h include in `#define private public`, as
  tests/lbfgsb_oracle does. None of them is linked into any guest ELF.
type: software
authors:
  - name: V-Sekai-fire
  - name: chibifire
references:
  - type: software
    title: interactor-aria-lbfgspp
    repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-aria-lbfgspp
    commit: 10086b6b2022802d7942ba16842c43063b3cff91
  - type: software
    title: interactor-tool-godot-cage-deformer
    repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-tool-godot-cage-deformer
    commit: f0b271620a4db16390101cc8ac2375c16680a9ab
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Biharmonic Coordinates and their Derivatives for Triangular 3D Cages
    authors:
